---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Ui.astro';
---

<Base title="Feedback">
  <h1>Feedback</h1>
  <p>
    Notices from the management. Alerts carry severity in the rule, waiting
    is a typewriter typing dots, progress is the ledger bar, an empty slot is
    a dashed tile, a toast is a telegram at the footlights, and the dialog is
    a playbill over the dimmed house.
  </p>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>NOTICES FROM THE MANAGEMENT</h2>
    <p>
      The rule carries the severity, not a pastel wash — a print shop tints
      with line and ink. Success prints solid: a thing done needs no colour.
      The warning notice spends the view&rsquo;s ochre ration.
    </p>
    <div class="demo-col">
      <div class="mk-alert mk-alert--info">
        <span class="mk-alert__title">Take notice</span>
        <span>The Tuesday matinee moves to three o&rsquo;clock, weather and Mr. Taylor permitting.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mk-alert mk-alert--success">
        <span class="mk-alert__title">Printed &amp; filed</span>
        <span>The new bill is at the printers; the Taylors have their box.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mk-alert mk-alert--warning">
        <span class="mk-alert__title">Attention</span>
        <span>The follow spot is running hot. Shorter solos are advised.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mk-alert mk-alert--danger">
        <span class="mk-alert__title">Trouble</span>
        <span>The trapdoor is stuck, and Act III depends upon it entirely.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mk-alert mk-alert--info">
        A single quiet line, without a kicker, works too.
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-alert mk-alert--warning"&gt;
  &lt;span class="mk-alert__title"&gt;Attention&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span&gt;The follow spot is running hot.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>TYPING DOTS</h2>
    <p>
      There are no spinners in a print shop. Waiting is a typewriter striking
      &ldquo;. . .&rdquo; one dot at a time on a stepped clock; under reduced
      motion the dots print once and hold.
    </p>
    <div class="demo-row demo-row--center">
      <span class="mk-spinner mk-spinner--sm" role="status" aria-label="Working"></span>
      <span class="mk-spinner mk-spinner--md" role="status" aria-label="Working"></span>
      <span class="wait-note">PATCHING THE PIPES</span>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;span class="mk-spinner mk-spinner--md" role="status" aria-label="Working"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE LEDGER BAR</h2>
    <p>
      Native <code>&lt;progress&gt;</code>: solid ink filling a 2px-ruled
      trough, advancing in stepped beats. The disk is at ninety-one percent,
      and nobody is taking this seriously. Omit <code>value</code> for the
      marching-hatch indeterminate state — work is happening, amount unknown.
    </p>
    <div class="demo-col">
      <progress class="mk-progress" value="91" max="100">91%</progress>
      <progress class="mk-progress mk-progress--sm" value="35" max="100">35%</progress>
      <progress class="mk-progress" aria-label="Setting the bill"></progress>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;progress class="mk-progress" value="91" max="100"&gt;91%&lt;/progress&gt;
&lt;progress class="mk-progress mk-progress--sm" value="35" max="100"&gt;35%&lt;/progress&gt;
&lt;progress class="mk-progress" aria-label="Setting the bill"&gt;&lt;/progress&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE DASHED TILE</h2>
    <p>
      An empty state is a dashed rule around typewriter text — nothing is
      printed here yet. No grey block, no illustration; speak in character.
    </p>
    <div class="demo-col">
      <div class="mk-empty">
        <span class="mk-empty__title">AN EMPTY SLOT ON THE BILL</span>
        <p class="mk-empty__message">
          No. 2 — coming soon. The second act signs on Thursday, or the
          chorus goes twice.
        </p>
        <div class="mk-empty__action">
          <button class="mk-btn" type="button">Book an act</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-empty"&gt;
  &lt;span class="mk-empty__title"&gt;AN EMPTY SLOT ON THE BILL&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;p class="mk-empty__message"&gt;No. 2 — coming soon.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;div class="mk-empty__action"&gt;
    &lt;button class="mk-btn"&gt;Book an act&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>TELEGRAM</h2>
    <p>
      A toast is a telegram slip delivered at the footlights: fixed
      bottom-center, one at a time — a new message replaces the old,
      telegrams never stack. It arrives in three stepped frames; gone means
      gone, with no exit animation. CSS-only: the app brings the timer and a
      hidden <code>role="status"</code> live region.
    </p>
    <div class="row">
      <button class="mk-btn" type="button" data-toast="">Send a telegram</button>
      <button class="mk-btn" type="button" data-toast="success">Delivered</button>
      <button class="mk-btn" type="button" data-toast="danger">Bad news</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-toast" hidden role="status"&gt;FILED · your note is on the spike&lt;/div&gt;

// app JS: show, wait, hide
toast.textContent = msg; toast.hidden = false;
setTimeout(() =&gt; (toast.hidden = true), 1800);</code></pre>
    <div class="mk-toast" id="demo-toast" role="status" hidden></div>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>PLAYBILL</h2>
    <p>
      Styling for the native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> — the one sanctioned
      modal: opened with <code>showModal()</code>, one at a time, never
      spawning another. The platform does focus trapping and Esc; the warm
      scrim dims the house, and the sheet drops in shot on twos.
    </p>
    <div class="row">
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--danger" type="button" id="demo-dialog-open">Strike the set&hellip;</button>
    </div>
    <dialog class="mk-dialog" id="demo-dialog">
      <h2 class="mk-dialog__title">STRIKE THE SET?</h2>
      <p>
        Two hundred four performances of flannel come down with it. The
        management advises a moment&rsquo;s pause at the fence before
        anything irreversible.
      </p>
      <form method="dialog" class="mk-dialog__actions">
        <button class="mk-btn" value="cancel">Keep it</button>
        <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--danger" value="confirm">Strike it</button>
      </form>
    </dialog>
    <pre><code>&lt;dialog class="mk-dialog"&gt;
  &lt;h2 class="mk-dialog__title"&gt;STRIKE THE SET?&lt;/h2&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;…&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;form method="dialog" class="mk-dialog__actions"&gt;
    &lt;button class="mk-btn" value="cancel"&gt;Keep it&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--danger" value="confirm"&gt;Strike it&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/form&gt;
&lt;/dialog&gt;

dialogEl.showModal(); // the app&rsquo;s one line</code></pre>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    // Toast demo — show/replace/hide; one telegram, per policy.
    (() => {
      const toast = document.getElementById('demo-toast');
      let t;
      const MESSAGES = {
        '': 'FILED · your note is on the spike',
        success: 'DELIVERED · the bill is at the printers',
        danger: 'STOP · the trapdoor is stuck again STOP',
      };
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-toast]').forEach((btn) =>
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          toast.className = 'mk-toast' + (btn.dataset.toast ? ` mk-toast--${btn.dataset.toast}` : '');
          toast.textContent = MESSAGES[btn.dataset.toast];
          toast.hidden = false;
          clearTimeout(t);
          t = setTimeout(() => (toast.hidden = true), 1800);
        })
      );
      // Dialog demo.
      const dlg = document.getElementById('demo-dialog');
      document.getElementById('demo-dialog-open').addEventListener('click', () => dlg.showModal());
    })();
  </script>

  <style>
    section.mk-card + section.mk-card {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-2xl);
    }

    .row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: var(--mk-space-sm);
    }

    .demo-col {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--mk-space-sm);
      max-width: 30rem;
    }

    .demo-row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: var(--mk-space-lg);
    }

    .demo-row--center {
      align-items: center;
    }

    .wait-note {
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono-sm);
      letter-spacing: var(--mk-track-back);
      color: var(--mk-color-text-muted);
    }

    pre {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-md);
      padding: 12px 14px;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      border-left: var(--mk-rule-thick);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono-sm);
      line-height: 1.6;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    code {
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: 0.86em;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      padding: 1px 5px 0;
    }

    pre code {
      background: none;
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-size: inherit;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
